data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

**Sync I/O via the Cosmos DB provider is fully removed.** In .NET 10 you could opt in to sync-over-async behavior, but in EF Core 11 that opt-in no longer exists. Calling any synchronous API **always throws** at runtime — no workaround.

Your affected calls:
- `ToList()` → use `await ToListAsync()`
- `First(...)` → use `await FirstAsync(...)`
- `Count()` → use `await CountAsync()`
- `SaveChanges()` → use `await SaveChangesAsync()`

**Fix:** Convert your repository to async:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
        => await _context.Products.ToListAsync();

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
        => await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
        => await _context.Products.CountAsync();

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

This will cascade through callers — they must also become `async`/`await` up to the controller level (which ASP.NET Core already supports natively).
